messages:
tara: opened a compact PR that adds guidance for mobile/edge clients + websocket vs HTTP streaming resume semantics, and clarifies how 429s, timeouts, and context trimming interact on flaky networks. includes tiny websocket/node snippets and a minimal repro harness for CI (mock ws server). PTAL :wave:

luc: link? want to review the websocket examples specifically. a lot of infra doesn't surface trailers or headers over ws frames, so we should document where to put resume cursors (frame metadata vs final close event).

tara: PR: https://github.com/redwood-inference/docs/pull/1142. I recommend placing resume metadata in the final frame as a small JSON envelope (some proxies strip HTTP trailers). added two patterns: 1) final-close event with opaque `resume_cursor`, 2) in-band metadata field on last chunk (for clients that only see frames).

indra: nice. ops ask for a short paragraph about billing: mobile retries can double-bill tokens if clients naively resend tails. please add a :warning: and a tiny example pattern to avoid dupes (checkpoint last-committed token id + idempotent tail).

tara: added cost warning and a tiny pseudo-code snippet for websocket resume: ```js
// ws resumable stream (pseudo)
ws.send(JSON.stringify({op: 'start', prompt, resume_cursor}));
ws.on('message', (m)=>{
  const ev = JSON.parse(m);
  if(ev.type === 'content'){
    if(ev.cursor <= lastCommitted) return;
    out += ev.text;
    lastCommitted = ev.cursor;
  } else if(ev.type === 'stream_close'){
    // optional resume cursor: ev.resume_cursor
  }
});
```

luc: couple of asks: 1) rename header/field to `x-resume-cursor` for telemetry parity, 2) add a one-line note about Dedicated queueing vs Hosted immediate 429s, 3) place ws snippets under examples/snippets/ws so importer picks them up.

tara: updated names to `x-resume-cursor`, added 'Deployment behaviors' bullet linking to dedicated docs (Dedicated can queue; Hosted may return 429), and moved ws snippet to examples/snippets/ws.

rafa: SDK team question: many SDKs currently auto-reconnect websockets. we should instruct SDKs to expose an explicit resume API instead of implicit reconnect, and show how to dedupe events client-side on reconnect. pls add a migration blurb.

tara: added migration guidance: "SDKs: avoid implicit websocket reconnects for streaming; expose explicit resume(cursor) and provide client-side dedupe using monotonic cursor IDs." included a tiny node snippet showing dedupe above.

indra: editorial: use code spans for header names (e.g., `x-resume-cursor`, `Retry-After`) and include a short matrix mapping observable outcomes to probable cause (sync 429 => rejected; mid-stream abort + 502/504 => server crash; mid-stream abort + resume_cursor => overload signal). Keep the matrix compact.

tara: updated formatting and added compact matrix. also added a short bit about trailers not reliably reaching mobile clients and why final-close events are safer.

docs-bot: CI checks started for PR #1142  link: https://ci.internal.redwood/1988.

luc: tiny nit: add explicit note about context trimming: checkpoint application-level commit points (turn ids) rather than raw token offsets to avoid mismatch when server trims prefix.

tara: added that. also included crosslinks to error-ref 429, SDK retry docs, and billing docs. ready for final thumbs. :thumbsup:

rafa: LGTM from SDK side; leaving final copy to indra.

indra: light edits for clarity. merge when CI is green. :shipit:

docs-bot: PR #1142 merged by indra at 1966667850."
